From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] user32, uxtheme, explorer, kernelbase, userenv, wldp, netapi32: small stubs that answered wrongly

- IsGUIThread said TRUE for every thread. A thread is a GUI thread once
  it has a message queue (win32u asks the server, which makes none); with
  TRUE it is given one. SHFileOperationW (which moves the operation off a
  GUI thread) now runs inline on threads with no queue, as it meant to.
- uxtheme's app and window dark mode calls kept nothing:
  SetPreferredAppMode (135) keeps the mode and gives back the old one;
  IsDarkModeAllowedForApp (139) is exported; AllowDarkModeForWindow (133)
  and IsDarkModeAllowedForWindow (137) keep a window property;
  FlushMenuThemes has nothing cached to flush.
- SHAppBarMessage ABM_SETAUTOHIDEBAR registered nothing: programs'
  auto-hide bars are kept, one an edge (the taskbar's own edge refused when
  it hides itself), ABM_GETAUTOHIDEBAR finds them, unregistering is for the
  bar itself, ABM_REMOVE drops a bar's registration; the EX messages
  (0x0b, 0x0c) are taken.
- AppPolicyGet* answered for any handle: the token is asked whether it is
  an app container's (packaged app answers then) and a bad handle is an
  error.
- GetProfileType took NULL (ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER now);
  WldpQueryWindowsLockdownMode likewise (E_INVALIDARG); FIXMEs gone.
- NetGetAadJoinInformation failed with ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED (as an
  HRESULT, a success code that is not S_OK): it gives S_OK and no join
  information, a machine joined to no tenant.

Wine's shell32 appbar tests: the todo_wine on
GetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID (fixed by 1620) is removed; no
failures.

Gate: test/guithread-gate.sh (Xvfb). Mutants SG_MUTANT_GUI_THREAD_ALWAYS
(win32u/message.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_DARK_WINDOW_STATE (uxtheme/system.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_AUTOHIDE_BARS (explorer/appbar.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_APP_POLICY_TOKEN (kernelbase/main.c),
SG_MUTANT_AAD_NOT_IMPLEMENTED (netapi32/netapi32.c).
